{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/stablegraphs\/stabledirectedgraph\/init(from:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"from"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"internalParam","text":"decoder"},{"kind":"text","text":": any "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Decoder"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Decoding allocates a page table entry for every page of 1024 positions from the first listed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position to the end, and a page for each page holding a listed element; positions before the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first listed one cost nothing. An end is implausible when that span is more than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"16 × count + 64","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" pages, where ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the number of vertices (or edges) listed: at most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"16 page table entries per listed element (about 2 KB for a vertex, 256 bytes for an edge)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plus 64. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"vertexEnd\": 4611686018427387903","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no vertices decodes, in O(1), while a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"payload cannot make decoding allocate without limit. A graph that has run more than that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"many empty pages past its live elements does not round-trip.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"maj